WEBVTT

00:00:05.900 --> 00:00:16.640
<i>Along a zigzag the world turns,</i>
<i>I heave out a sigh.</i>

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:27.660
<i>Someone pauses along the way,</i>
<i>but reality moves on.</i>

00:00:27.890 --> 00:00:33.190
<i>Treat love as love, treat</i>
<i>dreams as dreams.</i>

00:00:33.300 --> 00:00:38.700
<i>It's difficult to say it in earnest.</i>
<i>The times forge ahead, but...</i>

00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:43.680
<i>I want to make you happy...</i>

00:00:43.810 --> 00:00:49.410
<i>I'll do so like I do to</i>
<i>be myself. Yeah!</i>

00:00:49.510 --> 00:00:54.440
<i>I'll make you happy...</i>

00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:59.850
<i>I dedicate all that</i>
<i>I can do to you.</i>

00:00:59.960 --> 00:01:11.170
<i>Along a zigzag the world turns,</i>
<i>I heave out a sigh.</i>

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:23.410
<i>Someone pauses along the way,</i>
<i>but love doesn't stop for me.</i>

00:01:28.090 --> 00:01:30.820
As you may know, there was a coup d'état
in the middle east kingdom of Aburada.

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:32.810
"Bokuto Station"

00:01:32.810 --> 00:01:33.410
As you may know, there was a coup d'état
in the middle east kingdom of Aburada.

00:01:33.530 --> 00:01:40.120
The royal heir, Prince Saki Abdusha,
escaped from his country...

00:01:40.230 --> 00:01:42.670
...and has secretly been living
in exile here in Japan.

00:01:43.170 --> 00:01:45.570
Really? I didn't know
that at all.

00:01:45.740 --> 00:01:47.510
That's because it's a secret.

00:01:47.510 --> 00:01:48.560
Oh! Oh, yeah!

00:01:48.740 --> 00:01:50.940
And so, what has happened
to the Prince?

00:01:51.110 --> 00:01:54.200
He suddenly disappeared
this morning...

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:55.840
...and a missing persons
report has been filed.

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:57.320
Is it an abduction?

00:01:57.320 --> 00:01:59.220
No. It doesn't appear so.

00:01:59.380 --> 00:02:02.390
Couldn't he just be sightseeing in Tokyo?

00:02:02.390 --> 00:02:03.560
No way.

00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:07.180
Keep an eye out for him while on patrol.

00:02:10.030 --> 00:02:12.020
What a hassle!

00:02:12.130 --> 00:02:14.930
If he's already living in exile, why
would he suddenly disappear?

00:02:15.100 --> 00:02:21.040
That reminds me, I think I read that
his mother's half-Japanese.

00:02:21.210 --> 00:02:24.780
So Japan's his home, to some extent?

00:02:24.780 --> 00:02:26.740
Possibly.

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:28.410
He's just sixteen.

00:02:28.580 --> 00:02:31.380
Are you saying it'd be worth looking for
him if he was a debonair, older man?

00:02:31.550 --> 00:02:32.810
Well, of course.

00:02:32.920 --> 00:02:36.050
We should just leave
the kids to Yoriko.

00:02:37.690 --> 00:02:40.590
That reminds me... I didn't see
her today. Where is she?

00:02:40.760 --> 00:02:42.730
Must be her day off.

00:02:42.730 --> 00:02:43.790
What?!

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:48.400
Wow! What a gorgeous day!

00:02:48.500 --> 00:02:51.700
Perfect for my day
off! Lucky me!

00:02:52.270 --> 00:02:56.430
I'll go into town... Hang around...
Get something to eat...

00:02:56.540 --> 00:02:58.510
Do some window-
shopping...

00:02:59.680 --> 00:03:02.200
Maybe some man will
even hit on me!

00:03:02.310 --> 00:03:04.280
Yippee!

00:03:05.650 --> 00:03:10.490
FILE. 22
YORIKO NIKAIDOU'S
DAY OFF

00:03:23.570 --> 00:03:27.060
Not exactly the kind of place
I want to visit by myself.

00:03:27.610 --> 00:03:30.270
But maybe I'll meet
someone here.

00:03:30.440 --> 00:03:31.140
Excuse me.

00:03:31.140 --> 00:03:32.280
Yes?

00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:34.080
If you wouldn't mind?

00:03:34.080 --> 00:03:35.770
Yes? What is it?

00:03:35.950 --> 00:03:37.780
Would you take our
picture for us?

00:03:37.950 --> 00:03:41.890
<i>This is the story</i>
<i>of my life.</i>

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:44.040
Ready when you are!

00:03:47.960 --> 00:03:48.860
Look out!

00:03:52.360 --> 00:03:54.090
That's dangerous! You
wanna get hit?!

00:03:54.900 --> 00:03:57.830
If you want to cross, you're supposed to
press the button and wait for the light!

00:03:58.070 --> 00:03:59.700
"Wait"..."Press the button"
See? Like this!

00:03:59.870 --> 00:04:00.200
My hand.

00:04:00.200 --> 00:04:01.370
What?

00:04:01.370 --> 00:04:02.460
Let go of my hand!

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:05.010
Oops! I'm sorry! I just got
caught up in the moment.

00:04:05.980 --> 00:04:08.450
You can cross when
it's green.

00:04:08.550 --> 00:04:09.980
Are you listening
to me?

00:04:10.150 --> 00:04:14.810
This is the first time a woman has
ever held my hand.

00:04:14.990 --> 00:04:16.620
What should I do?

00:04:16.620 --> 00:04:18.990
Don't make a big deal about it.

00:04:19.090 --> 00:04:21.960
It was nothing. Think
of it as a dog bite.

00:04:22.060 --> 00:04:24.890
Hey, aren't you going
to cross?

00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:26.190
Huh?

00:04:29.170 --> 00:04:31.260
What a weird kid.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:38.330
Hmm... It still tastes good,
even if I am all alone.

00:04:38.440 --> 00:04:40.410
That boy sure was
a cutie, though.

00:04:40.510 --> 00:04:42.810
The first time he's held a
woman's hand, he says!

00:04:42.910 --> 00:04:44.680
I was more embarrassed
than he was!

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:47.410
He stiffed me!

00:04:47.590 --> 00:04:49.920
Someone didn't pay?

00:04:51.190 --> 00:04:52.350
Hey, that's him!

00:04:52.520 --> 00:04:53.760
Get your hands off me!

00:04:53.760 --> 00:04:55.660
Quit with the attitude, will ya?

00:04:55.830 --> 00:04:57.950
Excuse me? What seems
to be the problem?

00:04:58.130 --> 00:05:00.960
You wanna know what happened?
This kid stuffed himself...

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:03.070
...then tried to get away without paying.

00:05:03.070 --> 00:05:03.760
Really?

00:05:03.940 --> 00:05:05.560
Come on! I'm calling
the cops on you.

00:05:05.740 --> 00:05:08.300
Wait, let's talk about
this. Listen...

00:05:08.410 --> 00:05:11.400
...if you pay, I'll just pretend I
didn't even see this happen.

00:05:11.740 --> 00:05:13.110
I don't have any money.

00:05:13.110 --> 00:05:13.600
What?

00:05:13.780 --> 00:05:15.300
Come here! You're
coming with me!

00:05:15.480 --> 00:05:18.750
Oh, what should I do?
Umm... Hey, I know!

00:05:19.050 --> 00:05:19.750
Wait! Excuse me!

00:05:19.750 --> 00:05:20.550
Huh?

00:05:20.720 --> 00:05:22.980
Maybe he's got a good
reason for this!

00:05:23.690 --> 00:05:26.950
How would it be if
I paid for him?

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:28.360
Who, you?

00:05:28.360 --> 00:05:29.190
Yeah.

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:31.920
I don't really care who pays,
as long as someone does.

00:05:32.030 --> 00:05:33.630
You sure are kind.

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:35.430
How much do I owe you?

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:37.370
Including tax, it's ¥30,900.

00:05:37.370 --> 00:05:41.000
¥30,900?!

00:05:43.840 --> 00:05:46.310
Yes ma'am! ¥30,900!

00:05:46.410 --> 00:05:48.310
If someone pays, I'll forget the whole thing.

00:05:48.310 --> 00:05:51.080
Thank you very much. I'm very sorry.

00:05:51.180 --> 00:05:53.550
Hey! Give the man
an apology! Huh?

00:05:53.720 --> 00:05:57.180
If you're looking for that young
man, he's long, long gone.

00:05:57.360 --> 00:05:59.790
What?! How could he?

00:05:59.960 --> 00:06:01.250
Thank you very much.

00:06:08.030 --> 00:06:09.800
It's such a beautiful day...

00:06:09.900 --> 00:06:13.030
...I wish we could have just gone
for a drive somewhere!

00:06:13.200 --> 00:06:14.510
That'd be wrong.

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:15.730
Listen to you!

00:06:15.910 --> 00:06:20.810
I know you were wishing it was
Nakajima riding beside you!

00:06:21.050 --> 00:06:24.850
What are you talking about?
He's out on patrol!

00:06:25.380 --> 00:06:29.650
Patrol? What for? It's
totally quiet today.

00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.720
No news is good
news!

00:06:31.890 --> 00:06:34.480
It's like what the Chief
was saying about...

00:06:34.590 --> 00:06:39.330
...that Saki kid who went missing
and about the coup d'état stuff...

00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:42.160
I just can't seem to relate
to it all, you know?

00:06:42.330 --> 00:06:46.900
You're right. It must mean that Japan's
such a peaceful country.

00:06:49.640 --> 00:06:52.510
I wonder where
that boy went?

00:06:52.610 --> 00:06:53.580
Huh?

00:06:53.680 --> 00:06:56.370
Found him! And he's with
some of his friends!

00:06:56.950 --> 00:06:59.880
Maybe he'll pay me
back if I ask him.

00:07:00.380 --> 00:07:02.910
How're you going to pay
us off then, huh?

00:07:03.090 --> 00:07:04.760
Speak up, punk!

00:07:04.760 --> 00:07:06.090
And don't give us any lip.

00:07:06.260 --> 00:07:09.850
Oopsie. Maybe they're not
his friends, after all.

00:07:09.960 --> 00:07:11.490
Now what
do I do?

00:07:11.660 --> 00:07:13.220
I've had enough of
you, deadbeat.

00:07:14.830 --> 00:07:15.560
Huh?

00:07:15.730 --> 00:07:18.670
Hey! What do you guys
think you're doing?

00:07:18.770 --> 00:07:20.670
I don't think violence is the
way to solve things!

00:07:20.840 --> 00:07:23.900
You some kind of
friend of his?

00:07:24.340 --> 00:07:26.540
No. Nothing like that.

00:07:26.540 --> 00:07:27.610
Then take a hike.

00:07:27.610 --> 00:07:29.880
But I can't do that.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:34.210
Then are you going to deal
with us in his place?

00:07:34.390 --> 00:07:37.650
This punk bumped into us
and didn't even apologize.

00:07:38.090 --> 00:07:39.790
That's not good.

00:07:39.790 --> 00:07:40.760
Right.

00:07:44.830 --> 00:07:48.460
<i>I've got no choice. I'll just have</i>
<i>to tell them I'm a police officer.</i>

00:07:49.000 --> 00:07:51.470
Get a load of this,
you big thugs!

00:07:52.700 --> 00:07:54.140
That's a...

00:07:54.310 --> 00:07:55.670
No way...

00:07:55.840 --> 00:07:57.600
Well? Are you
worried?

00:07:57.780 --> 00:07:59.680
Yeah...

00:07:59.780 --> 00:08:03.210
...it looks like we have the same
"Keronpi" address book.

00:08:03.510 --> 00:08:05.910
Oops.

00:08:06.020 --> 00:08:07.210
<i>I forgot.</i>

00:08:07.320 --> 00:08:10.550
<i>I took my badge out</i>
<i>'cause I'm off-duty.</i>

00:08:10.720 --> 00:08:14.120
Hey babe, you just wanna exchange
addresses with me, don't you?

00:08:14.290 --> 00:08:15.120
That's not it!

00:08:15.290 --> 00:08:16.260
What?!

00:08:16.730 --> 00:08:20.090
Are you screwing
with us?

00:08:20.260 --> 00:08:23.320
You wench! You're not gonna
get away that easily.

00:08:23.500 --> 00:08:24.730
No!

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:26.570
Get your hands off of her.

00:08:26.570 --> 00:08:27.710
What's that, punk?!

00:08:27.710 --> 00:08:30.040
You're very annoying.

00:08:31.310 --> 00:08:32.870
Huh?

00:08:35.110 --> 00:08:35.810
Wow.

00:08:35.980 --> 00:08:36.550
What happened?

00:08:36.550 --> 00:08:37.670
He asked for it!

00:08:38.420 --> 00:08:41.390
Why you!

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:52.530
We'll get you
next time!

00:08:53.830 --> 00:08:55.990
Thank goodness!

00:08:56.170 --> 00:08:57.290
You all right?

00:08:57.470 --> 00:08:59.030
Yeah, I'm fine!

00:08:59.140 --> 00:09:01.970
Looks like you ended
up saving me, huh?

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:03.770
I do owe you,
after all.

00:09:04.710 --> 00:09:06.470
Oh yeah! The money!

00:09:09.180 --> 00:09:11.270
Where do you live?

00:09:11.380 --> 00:09:13.510
You can get some money
from home, right?

00:09:15.750 --> 00:09:16.820
I don't have a home.

00:09:16.820 --> 00:09:17.310
Huh?

00:09:18.560 --> 00:09:21.620
I don't have any place
to go home to.

00:09:21.790 --> 00:09:25.690
What do you mean? I
don't understand.

00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:28.900
You stay right there.

00:09:29.000 --> 00:09:31.130
If you try running away, I'll
put out an APB on you.

00:09:32.070 --> 00:09:35.630
Wait right there, ma'am! I'll
help you down the stairs.

00:09:36.210 --> 00:09:37.880
There. Watch your step now.

00:09:37.880 --> 00:09:40.110
I can't thank you enough!

00:09:40.110 --> 00:09:41.080
No trouble at all.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:43.380
Well, you're very kind.

00:09:43.380 --> 00:09:44.510
Nah...

00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:47.310
Thank you very much, for
helping me carry this!

00:09:47.490 --> 00:09:50.220
Not at all. Bye now.
Take care.

00:09:52.160 --> 00:09:54.560
My, am I thirsty!

00:09:54.660 --> 00:09:56.590
How about we get something
cold to drink?

00:09:56.760 --> 00:09:58.820
Yeah, but...

00:09:59.430 --> 00:10:01.560
Don't worry about
it. I'm buying.

00:10:12.440 --> 00:10:14.600
Ah! That hit
the spot!

00:10:14.780 --> 00:10:16.110
What a weirdo.

00:10:16.110 --> 00:10:17.380
Who is?

00:10:17.380 --> 00:10:18.280
You are.

00:10:18.280 --> 00:10:19.720
I am?

00:10:19.820 --> 00:10:22.180
Why do you say that? What's
weird about me?

00:10:22.290 --> 00:10:24.380
You're the one
who's weird.

00:10:25.060 --> 00:10:27.650
Why do you go around helping
out other people anyway?

00:10:28.190 --> 00:10:32.390
You're supposed to help people
who're in trouble.

00:10:33.260 --> 00:10:35.100
So you're saying it's altruistic?

00:10:35.100 --> 00:10:38.130
I wouldn't go that far...

00:10:39.040 --> 00:10:42.630
Don't you think altruism
is a little arrogant?

00:10:46.810 --> 00:10:50.410
Like I said... it's much
simpler than that.

00:10:51.520 --> 00:10:53.110
Will you throw our
ball back to us?

00:10:53.280 --> 00:10:55.150
Pretty please!

00:10:55.320 --> 00:10:56.980
Okay! Ready?

00:10:57.090 --> 00:10:59.060
Here goes!

00:11:00.390 --> 00:11:01.090
Thanks!

00:11:01.260 --> 00:11:03.390
Thanks, lady!

00:11:04.130 --> 00:11:05.960
What I mean is
that, well...

00:11:06.060 --> 00:11:08.660
...would you understand if I
said it was part of my job?

00:11:09.570 --> 00:11:10.360
Your job?

00:11:10.840 --> 00:11:14.200
That's right. I work at a place
called Bokuto Station...

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:16.710
...as a police officer. Fooled you, didn't I?!

00:11:16.710 --> 00:11:17.840
A police officer?!

00:11:17.840 --> 00:11:20.470
I guess I don't look the part, do I?

00:11:20.640 --> 00:11:24.050
Well, I do look like one when I have
my uniform on, that's for sure!

00:11:24.150 --> 00:11:27.240
I wish I could show you,
but today's my day off!

00:11:27.420 --> 00:11:30.350
It is? You mean you work
even on your day off?

00:11:30.920 --> 00:11:33.690
Yeah. It's hard to
shake the habit.

00:11:34.260 --> 00:11:37.390
In other words... I guess
you could say...

00:11:37.700 --> 00:11:41.150
...that I unconsciously go ahead
and do the things I ought to do.

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:44.360
"The things you
ought to do?"

00:11:44.840 --> 00:11:46.800
Right. That's
what it's like.

00:11:48.040 --> 00:11:49.800
<i>The things you</i>
<i>ought to do...</i>

00:11:51.310 --> 00:11:53.080
Are you all finished with your drink?

00:11:53.080 --> 00:11:54.770
Huh? Oh, yeah.

00:11:55.480 --> 00:11:59.750
I don't know why, but I just can't
leave you by yourself.

00:12:00.920 --> 00:12:02.780
I don't even know
who you are.

00:12:02.950 --> 00:12:04.890
At least tell me your name.

00:12:04.890 --> 00:12:06.520
Are you interrogating me?

00:12:07.190 --> 00:12:11.250
Hmm... Well...

00:12:11.760 --> 00:12:12.890
I know.

00:12:13.000 --> 00:12:16.400
Why don't we introduce ourselves
to each other, as friends?

00:12:16.570 --> 00:12:17.800
As friends?

00:12:17.800 --> 00:12:19.270
That's right. Friends.

00:12:19.970 --> 00:12:22.460
Then maybe you'll
open up, right?

00:12:22.640 --> 00:12:26.600
But we were holding
hands before.

00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:29.010
That's true.

00:12:29.180 --> 00:12:32.340
Don't I have to take responsibility
for my actions?

00:12:32.520 --> 00:12:36.040
Responsibility? I'm not
sure what you mean.

00:12:36.220 --> 00:12:37.960
Yeah, right. This is Japan.

00:12:37.960 --> 00:12:39.590
You mean?

00:12:39.590 --> 00:12:41.750
My name's Saki Abdusha.

00:12:41.930 --> 00:12:43.890
So you're not
Japanese?

00:12:44.060 --> 00:12:45.760
My mom was half-
Japanese.

00:12:45.860 --> 00:12:51.170
So, I'm part Japanese, even
though it's just 1/4.

00:12:51.340 --> 00:12:53.770
So is this your first...

00:12:53.770 --> 00:12:54.860
It's my first visit.

00:12:55.040 --> 00:12:58.530
I see. That explains all the strange
things you were doing.

00:12:58.710 --> 00:13:00.470
What's your
name?

00:13:00.910 --> 00:13:02.940
Yoriko. It's Yoriko Nikaidou.

00:13:03.580 --> 00:13:07.780
By the way, Saki... What were you doing,
walking around here, anyway?

00:13:07.950 --> 00:13:10.010
I'm looking for a building
called a shrine.

00:13:10.920 --> 00:13:12.660
A Japanese religious building.

00:13:12.660 --> 00:13:14.690
Religious building?

00:13:14.690 --> 00:13:16.490
Do you know of it?

00:13:16.490 --> 00:13:19.260
Yeah sure, but why?

00:13:20.330 --> 00:13:22.630
I need to pray about
something.

00:13:22.800 --> 00:13:26.760
I get it. You need to go there.
I'll show you the way.

00:13:28.410 --> 00:13:29.740
"Nagakawa Shrine"

00:13:37.720 --> 00:13:42.120
It's probably a little different from
what you're looking for, but...

00:13:42.290 --> 00:13:44.820
No. There is an air of solemnity here.

00:13:44.820 --> 00:13:46.480
That's good to hear.

00:14:13.320 --> 00:14:14.980
What's the matter?

00:14:15.150 --> 00:14:17.710
I wonder if my prayers
will be answered.

00:14:17.890 --> 00:14:19.790
You prayed, right?

00:14:19.960 --> 00:14:24.690
Yeah... but I'm only
1/4 Japanese.

00:14:24.860 --> 00:14:26.590
That doesn't make
any difference.

00:14:26.760 --> 00:14:28.300
You really think so?

00:14:28.300 --> 00:14:33.670
Sure. If you prayed from your heart.

00:14:33.840 --> 00:14:37.830
I wonder if my prayers will really
come true. And if they do...

00:14:37.940 --> 00:14:39.270
...I wonder...

00:14:39.380 --> 00:14:41.810
...if I should go back
to my own country.

00:14:45.180 --> 00:14:47.740
Where is your
country, Saki?

00:14:53.060 --> 00:14:55.060
A place that is nothing but sand.

00:14:55.060 --> 00:14:57.030
A desert country, huh?

00:14:57.130 --> 00:14:59.820
And did you pray to go
back there, Saki?

00:15:00.330 --> 00:15:03.030
It's not as simple
as that!

00:15:04.570 --> 00:15:05.800
Sorry.

00:15:05.800 --> 00:15:08.140
No, I'm the one who should apologize.

00:15:09.040 --> 00:15:10.510
I'm sorry.

00:15:10.670 --> 00:15:12.300
It's okay.

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:21.480
The government in my country
is very unstable these days...

00:15:21.590 --> 00:15:24.990
...and many people are
afraid for their lives.

00:15:25.090 --> 00:15:26.650
I was afraid, too.

00:15:26.760 --> 00:15:31.090
But some people saved my
life, and thanks to them...

00:15:31.200 --> 00:15:32.690
...I made it here
to Japan.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:34.930
That sounds terrible.

00:15:35.870 --> 00:15:39.060
But I don't know if things have turned
out the way they should.

00:15:39.170 --> 00:15:43.160
A while ago you said that you do
the things you ought to do.

00:15:43.640 --> 00:15:46.800
I guess I accidentally said
something profound.

00:15:47.540 --> 00:15:50.740
No... I think you
spoke the truth.

00:15:51.580 --> 00:15:54.420
There's something I should
be doing, too.

00:15:54.520 --> 00:15:56.710
But instead, I ran away
from my country.

00:15:57.820 --> 00:16:01.220
That's why I'm praying
from so far, far away.

00:16:04.060 --> 00:16:06.220
I want to go back
to my homeland.

00:16:07.460 --> 00:16:08.830
Saki...

00:16:14.170 --> 00:16:17.300
It's too difficult for me
to understand, but...

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:21.210
...maybe if you go back, everything
will work out okay.

00:16:29.450 --> 00:16:31.650
But it's not enough
just to go back.

00:16:31.760 --> 00:16:33.690
You have to really feel that
you want to go back.

00:16:36.430 --> 00:16:38.790
If you really want your prayers
to be answered...

00:16:38.900 --> 00:16:42.660
...then the first thing you've got
to do is take the initiative.

00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:43.800
Initiative?

00:16:43.970 --> 00:16:48.230
Yeah! Then you should
do what you have to do.

00:16:48.410 --> 00:16:50.410
"What I have to do?"

00:16:50.410 --> 00:16:51.940
"What I have to do?"
You want to do it, right?

00:16:51.940 --> 00:16:52.080
You want to do it, right?

00:16:52.080 --> 00:16:54.070
Yeah.
You want to do it, right?

00:17:07.120 --> 00:17:11.020
Master Saki!

00:17:11.200 --> 00:17:13.320
Are you all right? We've
been searching for you.

00:17:13.500 --> 00:17:15.430
Sorry I made you worry.

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:16.060
Huh?

00:17:16.770 --> 00:17:18.790
Everyone's waiting
for your return.

00:17:19.670 --> 00:17:21.640
Then let's go home.

00:17:22.040 --> 00:17:24.560
We'll take you back to the
hotel, Master Saki.

00:17:25.380 --> 00:17:26.270
No!

00:17:26.380 --> 00:17:27.710
I'm going back to my country.

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:29.110
Huh?

00:17:45.830 --> 00:17:47.230
Oh yeah!

00:17:47.330 --> 00:17:53.570
I forgot about the money!
What about my ¥30,900?!

00:17:56.340 --> 00:17:56.670
"Traffic Dept."

00:17:56.670 --> 00:17:58.770
What? He was
a prince?

00:17:59.180 --> 00:18:01.010
Are you serious?!

00:18:01.510 --> 00:18:03.380
I can't believe it!

00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:05.920
You can't believe it?!
What about us?

00:18:06.080 --> 00:18:08.140
I still can't believe you
two got together.

00:18:08.890 --> 00:18:11.620
It's once in a lifetime that you
meet someone like that.

00:18:11.790 --> 00:18:13.150
I think that it's
wonderful.

00:18:13.320 --> 00:18:15.420
The Prince
is leaving.

00:18:15.530 --> 00:18:19.360
He's going to come out of exile,
and return to his own country.

00:18:19.530 --> 00:18:22.500
What if the coup d'état is successful,
and the military takes control?

00:18:22.600 --> 00:18:25.300
What will happen?

00:18:25.470 --> 00:18:28.230
What'll happen to Saki?!

00:18:28.410 --> 00:18:31.200
He'll be arrested by the military,
and in the worst case...

00:18:31.310 --> 00:18:32.540
...he'll be executed.

00:18:32.980 --> 00:18:34.410
Executed?!

00:18:34.580 --> 00:18:35.640
How could they?!

00:18:35.810 --> 00:18:38.470
Then why would
he return?

00:18:41.050 --> 00:18:43.290
You're all wrong. He didn't give up.

00:18:43.290 --> 00:18:43.620
What?

00:18:43.790 --> 00:18:44.520
Nikaidou!

00:18:44.520 --> 00:18:45.580
Yes?

00:18:45.760 --> 00:18:49.160
The Prince says he wants to meet
with you before he leaves.

00:18:49.330 --> 00:18:50.660
Really?

00:18:50.830 --> 00:18:53.320
I order you to report to him
at one o'clock today.

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:55.470
Yes, sir.

00:19:08.110 --> 00:19:09.040
Yoriko...

00:19:09.150 --> 00:19:12.170
...l've decided to fight
for my country.

00:19:12.280 --> 00:19:15.580
It's up to me to protect the
people of my country.

00:19:16.050 --> 00:19:18.040
So that was what you
said you had to do...

00:19:18.160 --> 00:19:19.850
...when we were
at the shrine?

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:22.590
I wonder if my prayers
will come true.

00:19:27.630 --> 00:19:28.270
"Desert (Sa), Hope (Ki)"

00:19:28.270 --> 00:19:29.360
Desert Hope...

00:19:30.070 --> 00:19:33.590
That's one way you can write your
name in Japanese - "Desert Hope."

00:19:34.270 --> 00:19:36.830
You're the hope for your
country's future!

00:19:37.870 --> 00:19:39.500
Thank you, Yoriko.

00:19:39.680 --> 00:19:42.540
You've helped me come
to a realization.

00:19:42.710 --> 00:19:46.810
And that decision will guide
me for the rest of my life.

00:19:46.920 --> 00:19:49.010
All thanks
to you.

00:19:49.190 --> 00:19:50.190
Huh?

00:19:50.190 --> 00:19:51.420
What?!

00:19:51.590 --> 00:19:52.850
In my country...

00:19:52.960 --> 00:19:55.020
...men aren't allowed
to touch women...

00:19:55.130 --> 00:19:56.850
...until they are
married.

00:19:57.560 --> 00:19:59.360
Do you mean?

00:19:59.860 --> 00:20:03.360
The first woman he touches
becomes his wife.

00:20:03.770 --> 00:20:04.830
Really?

00:20:05.870 --> 00:20:07.630
But this is
Japan...

00:20:07.740 --> 00:20:10.640
I suppose such traditions
mean nothing here.

00:20:12.440 --> 00:20:15.310
Geez, Saki... You caught
me off-guard...

00:20:17.810 --> 00:20:22.510
Or will you come
with me, Yoriko?

00:20:22.920 --> 00:20:25.550
But I...

00:20:26.420 --> 00:20:28.020
I see.

00:20:28.690 --> 00:20:32.650
You have things you
have to do, too.

00:20:32.830 --> 00:20:34.820
Yeah.

00:20:35.700 --> 00:20:38.500
The next time I come
to Japan...

00:20:38.600 --> 00:20:41.300
...l'll be coming as a state
guest. At that time...

00:20:41.410 --> 00:20:44.470
...would you be my honored
escort, Yoriko?

00:20:44.640 --> 00:20:45.630
Yes!

00:20:45.740 --> 00:20:47.770
I would be honored,
Your Highness!

00:20:49.550 --> 00:20:57.950
<i>Sometimes love</i>
<i>can be Ionely...</i>

00:20:58.290 --> 00:21:06.920
<i>But if you believe...</i>
<i>it will shine through.</i>

00:21:07.260 --> 00:21:16.040
<i>What you and I have together</i>
<i>is a story so precious to me...</i>

00:21:16.240 --> 00:21:23.700
<i>I don't want it to become</i>
<i>just a memory.</i>

00:21:23.950 --> 00:21:33.050
<i>The river always flows...</i>
<i>Time flows...</i>

00:21:33.290 --> 00:21:40.660
<i>We'll stay the same</i>
<i>Just us two...</i>

00:21:40.800 --> 00:21:46.500
<i>No changing us.</i>

00:22:02.920 --> 00:22:07.920
<i>I live my life my own way, doing</i>
<i>things others wouldn't.</i>

00:22:12.260 --> 00:22:20.100
<i>Being strong isn't enough.</i>
<i>It makes me Ionely.</i>

00:22:22.810 --> 00:22:31.110
<i>I can feel your presence</i>
<i>as if you're right here...</i>

00:22:31.650 --> 00:22:39.220
<i>... but I can't say a word.</i>

00:22:40.760 --> 00:22:48.020
<i>The feelings I hide within might</i>
<i>break into pieces...</i>

00:22:49.500 --> 00:22:56.870
<i>But if I don't say anything,</i>
<i>nothing can begin.</i>

00:22:57.210 --> 00:23:04.440
<i>The wind gently blows...</i>
<i>Time flows...</i>

00:23:04.610 --> 00:23:14.160
<i>Time flows... And soon</i>
<i>I can be honest...</i>

00:23:14.290 --> 00:23:17.260
<i>Thank you,</i>
<i>friend!</i>

00:23:23.400 --> 00:23:25.230
"A Traditional Wedding"

00:23:27.140 --> 00:23:29.900
Oh, Nakajima's dad and Sena
are going to get married.

00:23:30.070 --> 00:23:31.340
That's right.

00:23:31.510 --> 00:23:33.070
I thought they'd already
gotten hitched.

00:23:33.240 --> 00:23:36.010
They've been busy moving
and opening the shop.

00:23:36.180 --> 00:23:37.540
Oh, how I wish it were
my wedding!

00:23:37.710 --> 00:23:40.480
Don't we dream about our
wedding dresses?

00:23:40.650 --> 00:23:43.350
Aoi, you're a man,
aren't you!?

00:23:44.220 --> 00:23:46.310
Next time, You're Under
Arrest, File 23...

00:23:46.420 --> 00:23:47.790
..."A Flower Blossoms
On The Virgin Road."

00:23:47.920 --> 00:23:49.860
I'm counting on
you guys.
